  "notes": "Term-by-term 'Sequence of Courses' transcribed from the official Arizona Western College Radiologic Technology program page, retrieved 2026-10-01. This is the PROFESSIONAL PHASE of the AAS (Major Code AAS.RADTEC): six lockstep semesters totaling 57 credits (2+13+13+5+12+12), matching the catalog's 57-credit professional sequence. Admission to the program requires a separate application AFTER completing 25 prerequisite credits (not in this plan): MAT 142 College Math with Applications or higher (3), ENG 101 or 107 Freshman Composition I (3), ENG 102 or 108 Freshman Composition II (3), PSY 101 Introduction to Psychology (3), AHE 101 Medical Terminology (3), BIO 160 Intro to Anatomy & Physiology (4; BIO 201 AND BIO 202 may substitute), an approved Institutions in the Americas course (3), and an approved Arts & Humanities course (3). Prerequisites require minimum grade C, minimum 2.50 prerequisite GPA, and completion within 5 years prior to applying. RAD 100 requires full acceptance into the program; each semester's courses must be completed before moving to the next. The full AAS degree totals 82 credits (25 prerequisite + 57 professional). Each clinical course carries an additional $1,150 fee; RAD 225 carries a $150 software fee. transfer_confidence is 'advisory': AAS/workforce professional-phase program; tccns mirrors the local AWC course code.",
